#
# Tests that the libcutils_test ctest entry leaves out.
#
# One test per line: the gtest name, a parity id and why it fails.  The
# parity id is a Linux system call from docs/specs/syscall-parity.md, or
# one of
#	abi:<name>	a row of docs/specs/abi-gap.md
#	tier0:<item>	something the tier-0 build does not have yet
#	env:<item>	a quirk of the FreeBSD dev VM, not of Android
#
# The tests of the files that system-tests.cmake does not build yet are
# here too, so that this file names every test that does not run.
#
# Tests that call GTEST_SKIP() on FreeBSD are not listed here.

AshmemMemfdCommonTests/AshmemMemfdTest.FileOperationsTest/Ashmem  tier0:ashmem-device  The test makes its region on /dev/ashmem.  Android 17 uses memfd (sys.use_memfd), and new apps cannot open /dev/ashmem; no FreeBSD ashmem device (gap register X8, owner decision 2026-10-19).
AshmemMemfdCommonTests/AshmemMemfdTest.ForkMultiRegionTest/Ashmem  tier0:ashmem-device  The test makes its region on /dev/ashmem.  Android 17 uses memfd (sys.use_memfd), and new apps cannot open /dev/ashmem; no FreeBSD ashmem device (gap register X8, owner decision 2026-10-19).
